.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-modules-cut 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-modules\-cut \- Move a closed set of crate\-root modules into a new sibling package, respelling every path, no shim
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten modules cut\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIfrom\fR> <\fIname\fR> <\fImodules\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move a closed set of crate\-root modules into a new sibling package, respelling every path, no shim
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print each path the cut would write or remove, and write nothing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIfrom\fR>
The package directory to cut from, relative to the workspace root (crates/batten)
.TP
<\fIname\fR>
The new package\*(Aqs name; it lands beside the one cut from
.TP
<\fImodules\fR>
The crate\-root modules that move, by name
